<h2>Glossary</h2>
<dl class="gl">
<dt>Chaturanga</dt><dd>"Four limbs": the four divisions of the army and the early form of chess.</dd>
<dt>Chaturangini Sena</dt><dd>The army of infantry, cavalry, elephants and chariots.</dd>
<dt>Padati / Ashva / Gaja / Ratha</dt><dd>Infantry, horse, elephant and chariot. They became pawn, knight, bishop and rook.</dd>
<dt>Vyuha</dt><dd>A battle formation.</dd>
<dt>Astra</dt><dd>A divine weapon in the epics.</dd>
<dt>Dharma-yuddha</dt><dd>A righteous war fought by rules.</dd>
<dt>Arthashastra</dt><dd>Kautilya's treatise on statecraft, economy and war.</dd>
<dt>Upaya</dt><dd>A method of dealing with others: sama, dana, bheda, danda.</dd>
</dl>
</div></section>

